# Own-wording spells of Deep Magic (2014 rules), chunk B (Bestial Fury to Caustic Torrent). TEXT = {name: text}.
TEXT = {
"Bestial Fury": "You fill a creature you can see within range with primal rage. The target makes a Charisma save and may choose to fail it. On a failed save it must use its action to attack the nearest enemy it can see, using unarmed strikes or natural weapons. While the spell lasts, its attacks deal an extra 1d6 damage of the same type as the weapon's damage, and it cannot be charmed or frightened. If no enemy is within its reach, it can use its action to repeat the save, ending the spell on a success. Undead and constructs are unaffected.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 3rd level or higher, you can target one additional creature for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Bewilderment": "You briefly dull the mind of a creature within range. The target makes a Wisdom save, and the spell does nothing on a success. On a failure, the next time the target makes an Intelligence check before the spell ends, it rolls a d6 and subtracts the result from the check. The spell then ends.",
"Binding Oath": "You seal a pact between two or more willing creatures through a ceremony of blessings that names the god of justice. The ceremony fixes both the terms of the oath and the penalty for breaking it, which is a curse. For each oathbreaker, you choose one of the curse options from the bestow curse spell. When a vow is broken, every participant instantly knows it happened but learns nothing more. Dispel magic cannot remove this curse. Dispel evil and good, remove curse, and wish can, but remove curse works only if its slot is at least as high as the slot used for binding oath. Depending on the oath, one creature breaking it may or may not free the others. If the oath is wholly broken, the spell ends for everyone, but curses already laid stay until removed.",
"Biting Arrow": "As part of casting this spell, you make a ranged weapon attack with a bow, a crossbow, or a thrown weapon. The attack's range is limited to 120 feet whatever the weapon normally allows, and you have disadvantage if the target is beyond the weapon's normal range. On a hit, the attack deals its usual damage, and the target is coated in thin frost until the start of your next turn. If the target uses its reaction before then, it takes 1d6 cold damage and the spell ends. The damage, both the attack's and the cold damage, rises by 1d6 at 5th level (2d6 total for each), by a further 1d6 at 11th level (3d6), and by a further 1d6 at 17th level (4d6).",
"Bitter Chains": "The spiked ring in your hand grows into a long barbed chain that wraps around a creature you touch. Make a melee spell attack against the target. On a hit, it is bound in metal chains for the duration. While bound, the target moves at half speed and has disadvantage on attack rolls, saving throws, and Dexterity checks. If it moves more than 5 feet during its turn, the barbs deal 3d6 piercing damage to it. The creature can use an action to break free with a Strength or Dexterity check against your spell save DC. The chains also release it if they are destroyed. They have AC 18 and 20 hit points.",
"Black Goat's Blessing": "You raise your splayed hand and speak a prayer to the Black Goat with a Thousand Young. Your magic gains an eldritch potency. Until the end of your next turn, the target has disadvantage on saving throws against spells you cast.",
"Black Hand": "You gather the power of darkness in your fist and hurl a paralyzing black flame at a target within 30 feet. If your ranged spell attack hits, the spell draws vitality out of the target and into you. For the duration, the target has disadvantage and you have advantage on attack rolls, ability checks, and saving throws that use Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution. At the end of each of its turns, the target makes a Constitution save with disadvantage, ending the effect on a success.",
"Black Hole": "You create a tiny black hole at a point you can see within range. It is a sphere with a 15-foot radius. Every fire within 40 feet of it, magical or not, is put out at once. Each creature within 40 feet when it appears makes a Strength save. On a failure, the creature takes 20d6 force damage and is pulled to within 5 feet of the hole. On a success, it takes half damage and is knocked prone but is not pulled. A creature within 5 feet of the hole at the start of its turn must succeed on a Strength save or take 8d6 force damage and have its speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. A creature within 40 feet but not within 5 feet at the end of its turn takes 2d6 cold damage. A creature reduced to 0 hit points within 5 feet of the hole dies at once.",
"Black Ribbons": "You pull strips of the plane of shadow into the world. They fill a 20-foot cube with inky ribbons that make the area difficult terrain and wind around nearby creatures. A creature that ends its turn in the area is restrained by the ribbons until the end of its next turn unless it succeeds on a Dexterity save. Once a creature succeeds on this save, the ribbons can't restrain it again, though the difficult terrain still affects it.",
"Black Sunshine": "You hold up a flawed pearl, which vanishes and leaves a magic orb in your hand that glows with dim purple light. Allies you choose become invisible while they are within 60 feet of you and the orb's light can reach their space. An invisible creature still casts a faint purple shadow. You can throw the orb as a weapon at an enemy. On a hit, the orb bursts in a flash and the spell ends. The target and every creature within 10 feet of it must succeed on a Dexterity save or be blinded for 1 minute. A blinded creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the blindness on a success.",
"Black Swan Storm": "You call up a whirlwind of black feathers that fills a 5-foot cube within range. Creatures in the cube take 2d8 force damage, or half as much on a successful Dexterity save. The feathers also give off darkness, so the light level within 20 feet of the cube drops one step, from bright light to dim light and from dim light to darkness. Creatures that save are still affected by the change in light.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 3rd level or higher, the feathers deal an extra 2d8 force damage for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Black Well": "You summon a churning sphere of dark energy 5 feet across at a point within range. It drags creatures in and drains their life. Each creature other than you that starts its turn within 90 feet of the well must succeed on a Strength save or be pulled 50 feet toward it. A creature pulled into the well takes 6d8 necrotic damage and is stunned. A successful Constitution save halves the damage and makes the creature incapacitated instead of stunned. A creature that starts its turn inside the well makes a Constitution save and is stunned on a failure or incapacitated on a success. An incapacitated creature that leaves the well recovers immediately and can act normally that turn. A creature takes damage only on entering the well, but it takes damage again if it leaves and is pulled back in. The well's extradimensional space holds nine Medium creatures, three Large creatures, or one Huge creature. When the spell ends, everything inside tumbles out and lands prone.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 7th level or higher, the damage increases by 6d8 and the pull distance by 5 feet for each slot level above 6th.",
"Blade of My Brother": "You touch a melee weapon that belonged to an ally who has died. It rises into the air and flies to another ally of your choice within 15 feet of you, entering that ally's space and moving along with them. If the weapon or the ally is forced more than 5 feet away from the other, the spell ends. On your turn the weapon attacks any target that presents itself. Its attack modifier is your spellcasting level plus the weapon's own magical bonus, if any, and it adds only its own magical bonus to damage. The weapon fights for up to 4 rounds, or until your concentration breaks, and then drops to the ground as the spell ends.",
"Blade of Wrath": "You form a sword of pure white fire in your free hand. It is the size and shape of a longsword and lasts for the duration. It vanishes if you let go, but you can call it back with a bonus action. As an action, you can make a melee spell attack with it. On a hit, the target takes 2d8 fire damage and 2d8 radiant damage. An aberration, fey, fiend, or undead creature that takes this damage must succeed on a Wisdom save or be frightened until the start of your next turn. The blade sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for another 20 feet.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 4th level or higher, either the fire damage or the radiant damage (your choice) increases by 2d8 for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Blazing Chariot": "You call on the power of angels to conjure a flaming chariot of gold and mithral in an unoccupied 10-foot square you can see within range. Two horses of fire and light pull it. You and up to three other Medium or smaller creatures you choose can board by spending 5 feet of movement, and the flames do not harm you. Any other creature that touches the chariot, or hits it or a rider with a melee attack from within 5 feet, takes 3d6 fire damage and 3d6 radiant damage. The chariot has AC 18 and 50 hit points. It is immune to fire, poison, psychic, and radiant damage and resists all other nonmagical damage. The horses are part of the chariot, not separate creatures. If the chariot drops to 0 hit points it vanishes and riders fall out. It has a speed of 50 feet and a flying speed of 40 feet. On your turn you can steer it instead of moving yourself. A bonus action directs it to Dash, Disengage, or Dodge. As an action, you can have it overrun creatures: this turn it can enter hostile creatures' spaces. Such a creature takes the touch damage, is moved to the nearest unoccupied space it can occupy, and must succeed on a Strength save or fall prone there.",
"Bleating Call": "You create a sound at a point within range. It can be any sound at any volume from a whisper to a scream, and it can continue unbroken or be made in separate bursts before the spell ends. Each creature that starts its turn within 30 feet of the sound and can hear it makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, the creature must take the Dash or Disengage action and move toward the sound by the safest route on each of its turns. When it reaches the source, it must use its action to investigate. After that it realizes the sound is an illusion and can no longer hear it, so the spell ends for it and cannot affect it again. If a target takes damage from you or one of your allies, the spell ends for it. Creatures that can't be charmed are immune.",
"Bleed": "Crackling energy coats one slashing weapon you are carrying. Until the spell ends, when you hit a creature with it, the weapon deals an extra 1d4 necrotic damage and the creature makes a Constitution save. On a failure, it gets a bleeding wound. Each time you hit a creature with this weapon while it has a bleeding wound, the weapon deals extra necrotic damage equal to the number of earlier hits you have landed on it with this weapon, to a maximum of 10. Any creature can use an action to staunch the wound with a Wisdom (Medicine) check against your spell save DC. The wound also closes if the target receives magical healing. Undead and constructs are unaffected.",
"Bless the Dead": "You bless one dead creature so it can cross into the realm of the dead in peace. A creature that receives this blessing can't become undead. The spell does nothing to living creatures or undead.",
"Blessed Halo": "A golden nimbus of light surrounds your head for the duration, shedding bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for another 20 feet. The spell gives you a pool of 10 points of healing. When you cast it, and as an action on later turns, you can spend points from the pool to restore that many hit points to one creature you can see within 20 feet. You also have advantage on Charisma checks against good creatures within 20 feet. If the halo's light overlaps magical darkness created by a spell of 2nd level or lower, that spell is dispelled.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 3rd level or higher, the pool increases by 5 for each slot level above 2nd, and the halo dispels magical darkness from a spell whose level equals the slot you used.",
"Blessed Rest": "You bless a creature to ensure a restful sleep. If the target takes a short rest, it can reroll any Hit Die it spends to regain hit points and keep the higher result. If it takes a long rest, it regains up to two extra Hit Dice, up to its maximum. For example, a target with eight Hit Dice could regain six spent Hit Dice after a long rest. Once the target has finished one rest of either kind, the spell ends.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 4th level or higher, you can target one additional humanoid for every two slot levels above 2nd.",
"Blizzard": "A howling storm of snow and ice crystals fills a cylinder 40 feet high and 40 feet across within range. Swirling snow heavily obscures the area. When the storm appears, each creature in it takes 8d8 cold damage, or half as much with a successful Constitution save. A creature makes the same save and takes the same damage when it enters the area for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there. A creature that takes cold damage from this spell has disadvantage on Constitution saves to maintain concentration until the start of its next turn.",
"Blood Armor": "When you hit a foe with a melee weapon attack, you can immediately cast this spell as a bonus action. You can't cast it any other way. The foe must have blood, or the spell fails. The blood flowing from the foe swells in volume and forms armor around you, giving you an Armor Class of 18 plus your Dexterity modifier for the duration. The armor has no Strength requirement, doesn't hinder spellcasting, and doesn't impose disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. If the foe you struck was a celestial, you also have advantage on Charisma saving throws for the duration.",
"Blood Lure": "You point at a place within range that holds at least a pint of blood, such as a jar, a bowl, or a puddle. Each creature that feeds on blood within 60 feet of that place, undead such as vampires included, makes a Charisma save. A creature with Keen Smell or a similar scent-sharpening ability has disadvantage on the save, and undead have advantage. On a failure, the creature is drawn to the blood and must move toward it unless something stops it. Once it arrives, it tries to consume the blood and takes no other actions while blood remains. A successful attack against an affected creature ends the effect for it. So does the blood being consumed, which takes the creature one action.",
"Blood Offering": "You touch the corpse of a creature that is not undead or a construct and consume its life force. You must have damaged the creature before it died, and it must have been dead no more than 1 hour. You regain hit points equal to 1d4 times the creature's challenge rating, with a minimum of 1d4. Only true resurrection or wish can restore the creature to life.",
"Blood Puppet": "Using a sample of a creature's blood, you control its body like a marionette. Choose a creature you can see within range and whose blood you hold. The target must succeed on a Constitution save, or you gain control of its physical actions for as long as you handle the blood component each round. As a bonus action on your turn, you can give it a simple, general order such as 'Attack that creature,' 'Run over there,' or 'Fetch that object.' If it finishes the order and gets no new direction, it defends and preserves itself as best it can. The target knows it is being controlled. At the end of each of its turns, it can repeat the Constitution save, ending the spell on a success.",
"Blood Scarab": "Your blood hardens into a ruby-like scarab that flies at a creature of your choice within range. The target must succeed on a Constitution save or take 1d6 necrotic damage. You gain temporary hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 2nd level or higher, you create one more scarab for each slot level above 1st. You can send them at the same target or different targets. Each target makes only one save, no matter how many scarabs aim at it.",
"Blood Spoor": "By touching a drop of your quarry's blood that was spilled or drawn within the past hour, you can follow its trail without fail across any surface or underwater, however fast you travel. If the quarry flies, you can follow its path along the ground, or through the air if you can fly. If it moves by magic such as dimension door or teleport, you sense its path as a straight line from where the magical movement began to where it ended, which may cross lethal or impassable barriers. The spell reveals the path of a creature using pass without trace. It fails against a creature protected by nondetection or by other effects that block scrying or make divination fail. If the quarry moves to another plane, the trail ends, but the spell picks it up again if you reach that plane before the duration runs out.",
"Blood Tide": "A creature you choose within range must succeed on a Constitution save or bleed from its nose, eyes, ears, and mouth. The bleeding does no damage but gives the creature a -2 penalty on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma checks. Undead and constructs are unaffected. A bleeding creature may draw the notice of blood-hunting animals such as stirges, sharks, or giant mosquitoes, as the GM decides. A cure wounds spell or a successful DC 10 Wisdom (Medicine) check stops the bleeding early. The duration increases to 2 minutes at 5th level, 10 minutes at 11th level, and 1 hour at 17th level.",
"Blood and Steel": "You cut your hand and take 1d4 slashing damage that can't be healed until you finish a long rest. Then you touch a construct, which must succeed on a Constitution save or be charmed by you for the duration. If you or your allies are fighting it, it has advantage on the save. Even constructs immune to being charmed can be affected. While it is charmed, you share a telepathic link with it as long as you are on the same plane, and you can give it orders without using an action while you are conscious. It does its best to obey. Orders can be simple and general, such as 'Attack the ghouls,' 'Block the bridge,' or 'Fetch that bucket.' If it finishes an order and gets no new one, it defends itself. As an action, you can take total, precise control of it. Until the end of your next turn it does only what you specify. In that time you can make it use its reaction, but that costs you your own reaction. Each time the construct takes damage, it repeats the Constitution save, and the spell ends on a success. If the construct was already under your control when you cast the spell, its Intelligence becomes 10 for 4 hours (unless it is already higher), and it can act on its own while staying loyal to you. You can also give it a bonus equal to your Intelligence modifier on one skill you are proficient in.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 5th-level slot, the duration is concentration, up to 10 minutes. With a 6th-level slot, it is concentration, up to 1 hour. With a slot of 7th level or higher, it is concentration, up to 8 hours.",
"Blood to Acid": "You choose a creature within range and turn its blood into virulent acid. The target makes a Constitution save. On a failure, it takes 10d12 acid damage and is stunned by the pain for 1d4 rounds. On a success, it takes half damage and is not stunned. Creatures with no blood, such as constructs and plants, are unaffected. If you cast it on a creature made mostly of blood, such as a blood elemental or blood zombie, the creature is slain if it fails the save.",
"Bloodhound": "You touch a willing creature and sharpen its sense of smell. For the duration, it has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell and on Wisdom (Survival) checks to follow tracks.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 3rd level or higher, the target also gains blindsight out to 30 feet for the duration.",
"Bloodshot": "You fire a jet of boiling blood from your eyes at a creature within 40 feet. You take 1d6 necrotic damage and make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 2d10 fire damage plus 2d8 psychic damage.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 3rd level or higher, the fire damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Bloody Hands": "You make the hands of a creature within range bleed heavily. These can be other fitting body parts such as claws or tentacles. The target must succeed on a Constitution save or take 1 necrotic damage each round and have disadvantage on all melee and ranged attack rolls that need its hands for the duration. While affected, casting a spell with somatic or material components requires a DC 10 Constitution save. On a failure, the spell is not cast but is not lost, and the casting can be tried again next round.",
"Bloody Smite": "The next time you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack during the duration, your weapon glows with a dull red light and the attack deals an extra 1d6 necrotic damage. Until the spell ends, the target makes a Constitution save at the start of each of its turns. On a failure, it takes 1d6 necrotic damage, bleeds heavily from the mouth, and can't speak clearly or cast spells with a verbal component. On a success, the spell ends. The spell also ends if the target or an ally within 5 feet of it uses an action to tend the wound and succeeds on a Wisdom (Medicine) check against your spell save DC, or if the target receives magical healing.",
"Bloom": "You can cast this spell only as a ritual. You plant a silver acorn in solid ground and spend an hour chanting praise to the natural world. Afterward, the land within 1 mile of the acorn becomes extremely fertile regardless of its former state. Seeds planted there grow at twice the natural rate, and harvested food regrows within a week. After one year the land slowly returns to normal fertility. Choose one of these effects, which appears and grows at once: a field of vegetables of your choice, ready to harvest. A thick forest of sturdy trees with plenty of undergrowth. A grassland with wildflowers and fodder for grazing. An orchard of fruit trees of your choice in tidy rows, ready to harvest. Living creatures that take a short rest in the area gain the maximum hit points from each Hit Die they spend. Bloom counters the effects of a desolation spell.\n\n**Ritual Focus.** If you expend your ritual focus, the duration becomes permanent.",
"Boiling Blood": "You make the blood in a creature's body boil with unnatural heat. Choose a creature you can see within range that is not a construct or undead. The target makes a Constitution save. On a success, it takes 2d6 fire damage and the spell ends. On a failure, it takes 4d6 fire damage and is blinded. At the end of each of its turns, the target can repeat the save. On a success, the spell ends. On a failure, it takes another 2d6 fire damage and stays blinded.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 5th level or higher, you can target one additional creature for each slot level above 4th. The creatures must be within 30 feet of each other when you target them.",
"Boiling Oil": "You conjure a shallow pool of boiling oil, 30 feet across, centered on a point within range. The pool is difficult terrain. A creature that enters it or starts its turn there takes 3d8 fire damage and falls prone. A creature that succeeds on a Dexterity save takes half damage and doesn't fall prone.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 3rd level or higher, the damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Bolster Undead": "You fill an area with negative energy that makes undead harder to harm or banish. Choose up to three undead creatures within range. When a target saves against being turned or against a spell or effect that deals radiant damage, it has advantage on the save.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 2nd level or higher, you can affect one additional undead creature for each slot level above 1st.",
"Bolstering Brew": "You call on the patron god of brewers to produce a small keg of vibrant beer or ale. Up to six other creatures within range can share the drink with you, each taking a mug from the keg. A creature that drinks a mug gains, for 8 hours, advantage on all Strength checks or on all Charisma checks (chosen when it drinks), immunity to being frightened, and advantage on all Constitution saving throws.",
"Bones of Stone": "The bones of a creature you touch take on the strength and density of stone. Until the spell ends, the target has resistance to slashing and bludgeoning damage and advantage on Strength checks against effects that would move it against its will.",
"Booster Shot": "You imbue a two-handed ranged weapon you touch, typically a shortbow, longbow, light crossbow, or heavy crossbow, with a random magical benefit. While the spell lasts, each projectile fired from it has an extra effect on a hit, in addition to its normal damage. Each time you cast the spell, roll a d6 to set the effect. 1: 2d10 acid damage to all creatures within 10 feet of the target. 2: 2d10 lightning damage to the target and 1d10 lightning damage to all creatures in a 5-foot-wide line between the weapon and the target. 3: 2d10 necrotic damage to the target, and the target has disadvantage on its first attack roll before the start of the weapon user's next turn. 4: 2d10 cold damage to the target and 1d10 cold damage to all other creatures in a 60-foot cone in front of the weapon. 5: 2d10 force damage to the target, which is pushed 20 feet. 6: 2d10 psychic damage to the target, which is stunned until the start of the weapon user's next turn.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 4th level or higher, all the damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Boreas's Breath": "You freeze standing water in a 20-foot cube, or running water in a 10-foot cube, centered on you. The water turns to solid ice. Its surface is difficult terrain, and a creature that ends its turn on it must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity save or fall prone. A creature partly submerged when the water freezes is restrained and takes 1d6 cold damage at the end of each of its turns. It can break free with an action and a Strength check against your spell save DC. A creature fully submerged when the water freezes is incapacitated and can't breathe. It takes 2d6 cold damage at the end of each of its turns, then makes a DC 20 Strength save, breaking free on a success. The ice has AC 10 and 15 hit points. It is vulnerable to fire damage, resists nonmagical slashing and piercing damage, and is immune to cold, necrotic, poison, psychic, and thunder damage.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 3rd level or higher, the cube grows by 10 feet for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Bottled Arcana": "You touch an empty stoppered glass container such as a vial or flask and enable it to hold one spell. To be captured, a spell must be cast intentionally into the container within 1 round of casting bottled arcana. The container can hold a spell of 3rd level or lower, for up to 24 hours. After that, the container becomes ordinary and the magic inside fades harmlessly. Any creature can use an action to unstop it and release the spell. If the spell has a range of self, the creature who opened the container is affected. Otherwise that creature picks targets as the spell's description allows. If a creature opens the container without knowing it holds a spell, the spell targets or is centered on that creature instead, whichever fits better. Dispel magic cast on the container targets bottled arcana, not the spell inside. If bottled arcana is dispelled, the container becomes ordinary and the spell inside fades harmlessly. Until the held spell is released, its caster can't regain the slot used for it. Once it is released, the slot is regained normally.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 6th level or higher, the level of spell the container can hold increases by one for each slot level above 5th.",
"Bottomless Stomach": "You gain the ability to swallow dangerous substances and hold them in an extradimensional reservoir in your stomach. You can safely swallow most liquids, including acid, alcohol, poison, and even quicksilver, and be unaffected by them. The spell grants no resistance or immunity to the substance otherwise. For example, you could drink a bucket of black dragon spittle safely but would still be burned by the dragon's breath or by the bucket being poured on you. The reservoir holds up to 10 gallons, and different liquids don't mix. Liquid beyond 10 gallons has its normal effect when you swallow it. At any time before you stop concentrating, you can use a bonus action to bring up 1 gallon of the stored liquid into an adjacent 5-foot square. A creature there must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity save or be affected by the liquid. The GM decides the effect by liquid type, using 1d6 damage of the fitting type as a baseline. When your concentration ends, the duration expires, or the spell is dispelled, the reservoir and its contents cease to exist.",
"Boulder Toss": "You draw on the strength of mountains and gain the power to hurl a rock or similar object as a giant does, using an action. For damage from objects you hurl, your Strength counts as 19. The thrown rock has a range of 60/240 feet and deals 2d10 bludgeoning damage on a hit. If the target is a creature, it must also succeed on a Strength check against your spell save DC or be knocked prone.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** If you use a slot of 4th or 5th level, your Strength counts as 21 and the bludgeoning damage becomes 3d10. With a slot of 6th level or higher, your Strength counts as 23 and the damage becomes 4d10.",
"Bouncing Fireball": "A bolt of flame leaps from your finger to a point you choose within range and explodes. Each creature within 20 feet of the blast takes 7d6 fire damage, or half as much with a successful Dexterity save. At once, a second bolt flies from that blast to a second point you can see exactly 40 feet from the first, and it explodes for another 7d6 fire damage with the same save. Then a third bolt jumps to a third point you can see exactly 40 feet from the second and explodes the same way. Each jump must be exactly 40 feet, no more and no less. If any part of a burst overlaps the area of an earlier burst, that burst doesn't happen and the spell ends at once.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 7th level or higher, the damage increases by 7d6 for each slot level above 6th.",
"Brawn Boost": "You touch a willing creature. Once before the spell ends, the target can roll a d6 and add the result to one Strength check of its choice, rolling before or after the check. The spell then ends.",
"Breathtaking Wind": "You hit a creature with a blast of wintry air. The creature must succeed on a Constitution save or be unable to speak or cast spells with a verbal component for the duration.",
"Breeze Compass": "You clearly picture or describe a location. You need not have been there, but it must exist on the Material Plane. Soon a gentle breeze rises and blows along the most efficient route to that place. Only you can sense it. At each decision point, such as a fork in a passage, you must succeed on a DC 8 Intelligence (Arcana) check to work out which way the breeze points. On a failure, the spell ends. The breeze steers you around cliffs, lava pools, and other natural hazards, but it does not avoid enemies or hostile creatures.",
"Brimstone": "You conjure a lump of sulfurous brimstone that appears in the air and drops to a point within range. A creature in that space must succeed on a Dexterity save or take 2d8 bludgeoning damage. The brimstone stays where it fell while the spell lasts. Each creature that starts its turn within 15 feet of it must succeed on a Constitution save or take 1d8 fire damage. The brimstone can be destroyed and has AC 8 and 12 hit points. It explodes if it takes fire damage. The explosion ends the spell and deals 1d8 bludgeoning damage to each creature within 15 feet, or half as much to a creature that succeeds on a Dexterity save.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 2nd level or higher, the fire damage increases by 2d8 for each slot level above 1st.",
"Brimstone Infusion": "You infuse an ordinary flask of alchemist's fire with magical brimstone. While infused, it can be thrown 40 feet instead of 20 and deals 2d6 fire damage instead of 1d4. The Dexterity check to put out the flames uses your spell save DC instead of DC 10. After 24 hours, the flask returns to its normal properties.",
"Brittling": "Biting cold makes a metal or stone object you touch brittle and easy to shatter. The object's hit points are reduced by an amount equal to your level as a spellcaster, and Strength checks to shatter or break it have advantage if made within 1 minute of casting. If the object is not broken in that time, it returns to its former state.",
"Broken Charge": "When an enemy you can see moves to within 5 feet of you, you speak a baffling word that bends its course. The enemy must succeed on a Wisdom save or take 2d4 psychic damage and spend the rest of its movement going in a direction you choose.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 2nd level or higher, the target takes an extra 2d4 psychic damage for each slot level above 1st.",
"Burning Radiance": "A line of light 60 feet long and 5 feet wide shoots from you in a direction you choose. Each creature in the line makes a Dexterity save. On a failure, it takes 10d8 radiant damage and catches fire. Until someone uses an action to put out the fire, the creature takes 1d10 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. On a success, the creature takes half damage and does not catch fire. The spell also ignites flammable objects in the line that aren't worn or carried.",
"By the Light of the Moon": "Magical moonlight fills the area within 30 feet of you. Besides providing dim light, it brings out hidden objects and places that hold useful clues. Until the spell ends, all Wisdom (Perception) and Intelligence (Investigation) checks made in the area have advantage.",
"By the Light of the Watchful Moon": "Whatever the hour or your location, you call on the moon's watchful gaze to expose threats to you and your allies. Shafts of bright moonlight, each 5 feet wide, shine down from the sky, or from the ceiling indoors, onto every space within range that holds a threat, whether an enemy, a trap, or a hidden hazard. An enemy that succeeds on a Charisma save resists the effect and isn't lit. The light doesn't make invisible creatures visible but shows their general position within the 5-foot beam. The light follows a target that moves, but a target that leaves the spell's area is no longer lit. Threats that enter the area after you cast the spell are not affected.",
"Call Shadow Mastiff": "You conjure a shadow mastiff from the plane of shadow. It obeys your spoken commands to help you in battle or to find a specific creature. It looks like a large dog with a smooth black coat, 2 feet high at the shoulder and weighing 200 pounds. It is friendly to you and your companions. Roll initiative for the mastiff, which acts on its own turn. It follows simple spoken commands within its ability, and giving a command takes no action. The mastiff disappears when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends.",
"Call the Hunter": "You split off a piece of your soul to become an embodiment of justice, a clockwork outsider called a summoned zelekhut. It serves you for the duration, as long as your commands fit its desire to punish wrongdoers. You can command it with a bonus action, and it acts immediately before or after you. The summoned zelekhut is a Medium construct, lawful good, with AC 19 (natural armor), 82 hit points (11d8+33), and a flying speed of 40 feet. Its scores are Str 21, Dex 11, Con 6, Int 10, Wis 17, Cha 15. It is immune to poison and to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical weapons. It is immune to the charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, and poisoned conditions. Its passive Perception is 13, and it speaks Celestial and Common. It has Magic Resistance, which gives it advantage on saves against spells and other magical effects. Its Multiattack is two Spiked Chain attacks. Each Spiked Chain attack is a melee weapon attack at +8 to hit with reach 10 feet against one target, dealing 14 (2d8 + 5) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) lightning damage.",
"Calm of the Storm": "While picturing the world as you wish it were, you lay your hands on a creature other than yourself and undo a chaos magic surge that affected it within the last minute. Reality reshapes as if the surge never happened, but only for that creature.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 4th level or higher, the time since the surge can be 1 minute longer for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Candle's Insight": "You cast this spell on a target as you light the candle used as its component. The candle burns for up to 10 minutes unless it is put out normally or by the spell's effect. While it burns, you can question the target, and the candle shows whether the target speaks truthfully. A deliberately misleading or partial answer makes the flame flicker and dim. An outright lie makes the flame flare and go out, ending the spell. The candle judges honesty, not truth. It burns steadily through even an absurd statement if the target believes it. This spell is used widely in society, by merchants in negotiation, inquisitors hunting heresy, and rulers interviewing foreign envoys. In some places, casting it on an unwilling target is a serious breach of hospitality.",
"Carmello-Volta's Irksome Preserves": "At your command, tasty fruit jam oozes out of a small mechanical device such as a crossbow trigger, a lock, or a clockwork toy. The device stops working until the spell ends and the device is cleaned with a damp cloth. Cleaning takes an action, but it has no effect until the spell ends. You can collect one serving of the jam in a suitable container. If someone eats it as a bonus action within 24 hours, it restores 1d4 hit points. The material component sets the jam's flavor. The spell can affect constructs with two limits. The target negates the effect with a successful Dexterity save. Also, unless the construct is Tiny, only one part of it (an eye, a knee, an elbow, and so on) can be disabled. The affected construct has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks that depend on that part until the spell ends and the jam is removed.",
"Catapult": "You magically hurl an object or creature weighing 500 pounds or less 40 feet through the air in a direction you choose, including straight up. Hurling an object at a specific target requires a spell attack roll to hit. A thrown creature takes 6d10 bludgeoning damage from the throw plus any fitting falling damage, and lands prone. If the thrown creature hits another creature, the total damage is split evenly between them and both are knocked prone.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a higher-level slot, each slot level above 6th increases the damage by 6d10, the distance thrown by 10 feet, and the weight limit by 100 pounds.",
"Catch the Breath": "You can cast this spell as a reaction when a breath weapon targets you. You have advantage on the saving throw against it. If you succeed, you take no damage, even if a successful save would normally halve it. Whether you succeed or fail, you absorb and store energy from the attack. On your next turn, as a bonus action, you can make a ranged spell attack against a target within 60 feet. On a hit, the target takes 3d10 force damage. If you choose not to attack, the stored energy fades harmlessly.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 4th level or higher, the attack's damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Caustic Blood": "Your blood turns caustic in the open air. When you take piercing or slashing damage, you can use your reaction to choose up to three creatures within 30 feet of you. Each target takes 1d10 acid damage unless it succeeds on a Dexterity save.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you use a slot of 3rd level or higher, you can choose one more target for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Caustic Torrent": "A swirling jet of acid sprays from you in a direction you choose, filling a line 60 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line makes a Dexterity save and takes 14d6 acid damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this spell is killed and its body liquefies. The line also releases toxic fumes. Each creature other than you that is in the line or within 5 feet of it is poisoned for 1 minute. Creatures that don't breathe or are immune to acid damage aren't poisoned. A poisoned creature can make a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.",
}
